#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Um curso gratuito da IBM sobre informação e computação quântica"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game"
msgstr "Jogo CHSH"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"The last example to be discussed in this lesson is not a protocol, but a *game* known as the\n"
"*CHSH game*.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"O último exemplo a ser discutido nesta lição não é um protocolo, mas um *jogo* conhecido como o\n"
"*jogo CHSH*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we speak of a game in this context, we're not talking about something that's meant to be played for fun or sport, but rather a mathematical abstraction in the sense of *game theory*.\n"
"Mathematical abstractions of games are studied in economics and computer science, for instance, and they are both fascinating and useful.\n"
msgstr ""
"Quando falamos de um jogo neste contexto, não estamos nos referindo a algo feito para diversão ou esporte, mas sim a uma abstração matemática no sentido da *teoria dos jogos*.\n"
"Abstrações matemáticas de jogos são estudadas em economia e ciência da computação, por exemplo, e são ao mesmo tempo fascinantes e úteis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The letters CHSH refer to the authors — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, and Richard Holt — of a 1969 paper where the example was first described.\n"
"They did not describe the example as a game, but rather as an experiment.\n"
"Its description as a game, however, is both natural and intuitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"As letras CHSH referem-se aos autores — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony e Richard Holt — de um artigo de 1969 no qual o exemplo foi descrito pela primeira vez.\n"
"Eles não descreveram o exemplo como um jogo, mas sim como um experimento.\n"
"Sua descrição como jogo, no entanto, é ao mesmo tempo natural e intuitiva.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game falls within a class of games known as *nonlocal games*.\n"
"Nonlocal games are incredibly interesting and have deep connections to physics, computer science, and mathematics — holding mysteries that still remain unsolved.\n"
"We'll begin the section by explaining what nonlocal games are, and then we'll focus in on the CHSH game and what makes it interesting.\n"
msgstr ""
"O jogo CHSH pertence a uma classe de jogos conhecidos como *jogos não-locais*.\n"
"Jogos não-locais são incrivelmente interessantes e têm conexões profundas com física, ciência da computação e matemática — guardando mistérios que ainda permanecem sem solução.\n"
"Vamos começar esta seção explicando o que são jogos não-locais e, em seguida, focaremos no jogo CHSH e no que o torna interessante.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Nonlocal games {#nonlocal-games}"
msgstr "Jogos não-locais {#nonlocal-games}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A nonlocal game is a *cooperative game* where two players, Alice and Bob, work together to achieve a particular outcome.\n"
"The game is run by a *referee*, who behaves according to strict guidelines that are known to Alice and Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Um jogo não-local é um *jogo cooperativo* no qual dois jogadores, Alice e Bob, trabalham juntos para alcançar um resultado específico.\n"
"O jogo é conduzido por um *árbitro*, que age de acordo com diretrizes rígidas conhecidas por Alice e Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can prepare for the game however they choose, but once the game starts they are *forbidden from communicating*.\n"
"We might imagine the game taking place in a secure facility of some sort — as if the referee is playing the role of a detective and Alice and Bob are suspects being interrogated in different rooms.\n"
"But another way to think about the set-up is that Alice and Bob are separated by a vast distance, and communication is prohibited because the speed of light doesn't allow for it within the running time of the game.\n"
"That is to say, if Alice tries to send a message to Bob, the game will be over by the time he receives it, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice e Bob podem se preparar para o jogo da maneira que escolherem, mas uma vez que o jogo começa, eles estão *proibidos de se comunicar*.\n"
"Podemos imaginar o jogo acontecendo em algum tipo de instalação segura — como se o árbitro estivesse no papel de um detetive e Alice e Bob fossem suspeitos sendo interrogados em salas separadas.\n"
"Mas outra forma de pensar sobre a configuração é que Alice e Bob estão separados por uma grande distância, e a comunicação é proibida porque a velocidade da luz não a permite dentro do tempo de execução do jogo.\n"
"Ou seja, se Alice tentar enviar uma mensagem para Bob, o jogo já terá terminado quando ele a receber, e vice-versa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way a nonlocal game works is that the referee first asks each of Alice and Bob a question.\n"
"We'll use the letter $x$ to refer to Alice's question and $y$ to refer to Bob's question.\n"
"Here we're thinking of $x$ and $y$ as being classical states, and in the CHSH game $x$ and $y$ are bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"A maneira como um jogo não-local funciona é que o árbitro primeiro faz uma pergunta para cada um de Alice e Bob.\n"
"Usaremos a letra $x$ para se referir à pergunta de Alice e $y$ para a pergunta de Bob.\n"
"Aqui estamos pensando em $x$ e $y$ como estados clássicos, e no jogo CHSH $x$ e $y$ são bits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee uses *randomness* to select these questions.\n"
"To be precise, there is some probability $p(x,y)$ associated with each possible pair $(x,y)$ of questions, and the referee has vowed to choose the questions randomly, at the time of the game, in this way.\n"
"Everyone, including Alice and Bob, knows these probabilities — but nobody knows specifically which pair $(x,y)$ will be chosen until the game begins.\n"
msgstr ""
"O árbitro usa *aleatoriedade* para selecionar essas perguntas.\n"
"Para ser preciso, há uma probabilidade $p(x,y)$ associada a cada par possível $(x,y)$ de perguntas, e o árbitro se comprometeu a escolher as perguntas aleatoriamente, no momento do jogo, dessa forma.\n"
"Todos, incluindo Alice e Bob, conhecem essas probabilidades — mas ninguém sabe especificamente qual par $(x,y)$ será escolhido até que o jogo comece.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After Alice and Bob receive their questions, they must then provide answers: Alice's answer is $a$ and Bob's answer is $b.$\n"
"Again, these are classical states in general, and bits in the CHSH game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Depois que Alice e Bob recebem suas perguntas, eles devem fornecer respostas: a resposta de Alice é $a$ e a resposta de Bob é $b.$\n"
"Novamente, esses são estados clássicos em geral, e bits no jogo CHSH.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point the referee makes a decision: Alice and Bob either *win* or *lose* depending on whether or not the pair of answers $(a,b)$ is deemed correct for the pair of questions $(x,y)$ according to some fixed set of rules.\n"
"Different rules mean different games, and the rules for the CHSH game specifically are described in the section following this one.\n"
"As was already suggested, the rules are known to everyone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Neste ponto o árbitro toma uma decisão: Alice e Bob *ganham* ou *perdem* dependendo se o par de respostas $(a,b)$ é considerado correto para o par de perguntas $(x,y)$ de acordo com um conjunto fixo de regras.\n"
"Regras diferentes significam jogos diferentes, e as regras do jogo CHSH especificamente são descritas na seção seguinte.\n"
"Como já foi sugerido, as regras são conhecidas por todos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following diagram provides a graphic representation of the "
"interactions.\n"
msgstr "O diagrama a seguir fornece uma representação gráfica das interações.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is the uncertainty about which questions will be asked, and specifically "
"the fact that each player doesn't know the other player's question, that "
"makes nonlocal games challenging for Alice and Bob — just like colluding "
"suspects in different rooms trying to keep their story straight.\n"
msgstr ""
"É a incerteza sobre quais perguntas serão feitas, e especificamente o fato "
"de que cada jogador não conhece a pergunta do outro, que torna os jogos não-"
"locais desafiadores para Alice e Bob — como suspeitos conluiados em salas "
"diferentes tentando manter a história coerente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A precise description of the referee defines an instance of a nonlocal game.\n"
"This includes a specification of the probabilities $p(x,y)$ for each question pair along with the rules\n"
"that determine whether each pair of answers $(a,b)$ wins or loses for each possible question pair $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Uma descrição precisa do árbitro define uma instância de um jogo não-local.\n"
"Isso inclui uma especificação das probabilidades $p(x,y)$ para cada par de perguntas, juntamente com as regras\n"
"que determinam se cada par de respostas $(a,b)$ vence ou perde para cada par de perguntas possível $(x,y).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll take a look at the CHSH game momentarily, but before that let us briefly acknowledge that it's also interesting to consider other nonlocal games.\n"
"It's extremely interesting, in fact, and there are some nonlocal games for which it's currently not known how well Alice and Bob can play using entanglement.\n"
"The set-up is simple, but there's complexity at work — and for some games it can be impossibly difficult to compute best or near-best strategies for Alice and Bob.\n"
"This is the mind-blowing nature of the non-local games model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Vamos dar uma olhada no jogo CHSH em breve, mas antes disso vamos reconhecer brevemente que também é interessante considerar outros jogos não-locais.\n"
"É extremamente interessante, de fato, e há alguns jogos não-locais para os quais atualmente não se sabe quão bem Alice e Bob podem jogar usando entrelaçamento.\n"
"A configuração é simples, mas há complexidade em ação — e para alguns jogos pode ser impossível calcular as melhores estratégias ou estratégias próximas das melhores para Alice e Bob.\n"
"Esta é a natureza surpreendente do modelo de jogos não-locais.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game description {#chsh-game-description}"
msgstr "Descrição do jogo CHSH {#chsh-game-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is the precise description of the CHSH game, where (as above) $x$ is "
"Alice's question, $y$ is Bob's question, $a$ is Alice's answer, and $b$ is "
"Bob's answer:\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui está a descrição precisa do jogo CHSH, onde (como acima) $x$ é a "
"pergunta de Alice, $y$ é a pergunta de Bob, $a$ é a resposta de Alice e $b$ "
"é a resposta de Bob:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The questions and answers are all bits: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
msgstr "As perguntas e respostas são todas bits: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee chooses the questions $(x,y)$ *uniformly at random*. That is, "
"each of the four possibilities, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ and $(1,1),$ is "
"selected with probability $1/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"O árbitro escolhe as perguntas $(x,y)$ *uniformemente ao acaso*. Ou seja, "
"cada uma das quatro possibilidades, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ e $(1,1),$ é "
"selecionada com probabilidade $1/4.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answers $(a,b)$ *win* for the questions $(x,y)$ if $a\\oplus b = "
"x\\wedge y$ and *lose* otherwise. The following table expresses this rule by"
" listing the winning and losing conditions on the answers $(a,b)$ for each "
"pair of questions $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"As respostas $(a,b)$ *vencem* para as perguntas $(x,y)$ se $a\\oplus b = "
"x\\wedge y$ e *perdem* caso contrário. A tabela a seguir expressa essa regra"
" listando as condições de vitória e derrota nas respostas $(a,b)$ para cada "
"par de perguntas $(x,y).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Limitation of classical strategies {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"
msgstr ""
"Limitação das estratégias clássicas {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's consider strategies for Alice and Bob in the CHSH game, beginning "
"with *classical* strategies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Agora vamos considerar estratégias para Alice e Bob no jogo CHSH, começando "
"com estratégias *clássicas*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deterministic strategies {#deterministic-strategies}"
msgstr "Estratégias determinísticas {#deterministic-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll start with *deterministic* strategies, where Alice's answer $a$ is a function of the question $x$ that she receives, and likewise Bob's answer $b$ is a function of the question $y$ he receives.\n"
"So, for instance, we may write $a(0)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $0,$ and $a(1)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Vamos começar com estratégias *determinísticas*, onde a resposta $a$ de Alice é uma função da pergunta $x$ que ela recebe, e da mesma forma a resposta $b$ de Bob é uma função da pergunta $y$ que ele recebe.\n"
"Portanto, por exemplo, podemos escrever $a(0)$ para representar a resposta de Alice quando sua pergunta é $0,$ e $a(1)$ para representar a resposta de Alice quando sua pergunta é $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No deterministic strategy can possibly win the CHSH game every time.\n"
"One way to reason this is simply to go one-by-one through all of the possible deterministic strategies and check that every one of them loses for at least one of the four possible question pairs.\n"
"Alice and Bob can each choose from four possible functions from one bit to one bit — which we encountered back in the first lesson of the course — so there are $16$ different deterministic strategies in total to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nenhuma estratégia determinística pode vencer o jogo CHSH em todas as vezes.\n"
"Uma maneira de raciocinar é simplesmente ir uma a uma por todas as estratégias determinísticas possíveis e verificar que cada uma delas perde para pelo menos um dos quatro pares de perguntas possíveis.\n"
"Alice e Bob podem cada um escolher entre quatro funções possíveis de um bit para um bit — que encontramos anteriormente na primeira lição do curso — portanto, há $16$ estratégias determinísticas diferentes no total para verificar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also reason this analytically.\n"
"If Alice and Bob's strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,0),$ then it must be that $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"if their strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,1),$ then $a(0) = b(1);$ and similarly,\n"
"if the strategy wins for $(x,y)=(1,0)$ then $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"So, if their strategy wins for all three possibilities, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Também podemos raciocinar analiticamente.\n"
"Se a estratégia de Alice e Bob vence quando $(x,y) = (0,0),$ então deve ser que $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"se a estratégia vence quando $(x,y) = (0,1),$ então $a(0) = b(1);$ e da mesma forma,\n"
"se a estratégia vence para $(x,y)=(1,0)$ então $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"Portanto, se a estratégia vence para as três possibilidades, então\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that the strategy loses in the final case $(x,y) = (1,1),$ for here winning requires that\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Thus, there can be no deterministic strategy that wins every time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isso implica que a estratégia perde no caso final $(x,y) = (1,1),$ pois aqui vencer requer que\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Portanto, não pode haver uma estratégia determinística que vença em todas as vezes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it is easy to find deterministic strategies that win in three of the four cases, such as $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"From this we conclude that the maximum probability for Alice and Bob to win using a deterministic strategy is $3/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Por outro lado, é fácil encontrar estratégias determinísticas que vençam em três dos quatro casos, como $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"Disso concluímos que a probabilidade máxima para Alice e Bob vencerem usando uma estratégia determinística é $3/4.$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic strategies {#probabilistic-strategies}"
msgstr "Estratégias probabilísticas {#probabilistic-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we just concluded, Alice and Bob cannot do better than winning the CHSH game 75% of the time using a deterministic strategy.\n"
"But what about a probabilistic strategy?\n"
"Could it help Alice and Bob to use randomness — including the possibility of *shared randomness*, where their random choices are correlated?\n"
msgstr ""
"Como acabamos de concluir, Alice e Bob não podem ir além de vencer o jogo CHSH 75% das vezes usando uma estratégia determinística.\n"
"Mas e quanto a uma estratégia probabilística?\n"
"Poderia ser útil para Alice e Bob usar aleatoriedade — incluindo a possibilidade de *aleatoriedade compartilhada*, onde suas escolhas aleatórias são correlacionadas?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It turns out that probabilistic strategies don't help at all to increase the probability that Alice and Bob win.\n"
"This is because every probabilistic strategy can alternatively be viewed as a random selection of a deterministic strategy, just like probabilistic operations can be viewed as random selections of deterministic operations.\n"
"The average is never larger than the maximum, and so it follows that probabilistic strategies don't offer any advantage in terms of their overall winning probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"Acontece que estratégias probabilísticas não ajudam em nada a aumentar a probabilidade de Alice e Bob vencerem.\n"
"Isso ocorre porque toda estratégia probabilística pode ser alternativamente vista como uma seleção aleatória de uma estratégia determinística, assim como operações probabilísticas podem ser vistas como seleções aleatórias de operações determinísticas.\n"
"A média nunca é maior que o máximo, e portanto segue-se que estratégias probabilísticas não oferecem nenhuma vantagem em termos de probabilidade de vitória geral.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, winning with probability $3/4$ is the best that Alice and Bob can do "
"using any classical strategy, whether deterministic or probabilistic.\n"
msgstr ""
"Assim, vencer com probabilidade $3/4$ é o melhor que Alice e Bob podem fazer"
" usando qualquer estratégia clássica, seja determinística ou "
"probabilística.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game strategy {#chsh-game-strategy}"
msgstr "Estratégia para o jogo CHSH {#chsh-game-strategy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural question to ask at this point is whether Alice and Bob can do any better using a *quantum* strategy.\n"
"In particular, if they share an entangled quantum state as the following figure suggests, which they could have prepared prior to playing the game, can they increase their winning probability?\n"
msgstr ""
"Uma pergunta natural a se fazer neste ponto é se Alice e Bob podem fazer melhor usando uma estratégia *quântica*.\n"
"Em particular, se eles compartilham um estado quântico entrelaçado como sugere a figura a seguir, que poderiam ter preparado antes de jogar o jogo, eles podem aumentar sua probabilidade de vitória?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game-entanglement.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game-entanglement.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is yes, and this is the main point of the example and why it's so interesting.\n"
"So let's see exactly how Alice and Bob can do better in this game using entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"A resposta é sim, e este é o ponto principal do exemplo e por que é tão interessante.\n"
"Então vamos ver exatamente como Alice e Bob podem se sair melhor neste jogo usando entrelaçamento.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Required vectors and matrices {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"
msgstr "Vetores e matrizes necessários {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first thing we need to do is to define a qubit state vector $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ for each real number\n"
"$\\theta$ (which we'll think of as an angle measured in radians) as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"A primeira coisa que precisamos fazer é definir um vetor de estado qubit $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ para cada número real\n"
"$\\theta$ (que vamos pensar como um ângulo medido em radianos) da seguinte forma.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are some simple examples:\n"
msgstr "Aqui estão alguns exemplos simples:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have the following examples, which arise in the analysis below:\n"
msgstr "Também temos os exemplos a seguir, que surgem na análise abaixo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Looking at the general form, we see that the inner product between any two "
"of these vectors has this formula:\n"
msgstr ""
"Olhando para a forma geral, vemos que o produto interno entre quaisquer dois"
" desses vetores tem esta fórmula:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In detail, there are only real number entries in these vectors, so there are no complex conjugates to worry about:\n"
"the inner product is the product of the cosines plus the product of the sines.\n"
"Using one of the *angle addition formulas* from trigonometry leads to the simplification above.\n"
"This formula reveals the geometric interpretation of the inner product between real unit vectors as the cosine of the angle between them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Em detalhes, há apenas entradas de números reais nesses vetores, portanto não há conjugados complexos com os quais se preocupar:\n"
"o produto interno é o produto dos cossenos mais o produto dos senos.\n"
"Usando uma das *fórmulas de adição de ângulos* da trigonometria leva à simplificação acima.\n"
"Esta fórmula revela a interpretação geométrica do produto interno entre vetores unitários reais como o cosseno do ângulo entre eles.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we compute the inner product of the *tensor product* of any two of these "
"vectors with the $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ state, we obtain a similar "
"expression, except that it has a $\\sqrt{2}$ in the denominator:\n"
msgstr ""
"Se calcularmos o produto interno do *produto tensorial* de quaisquer dois "
"desses vetores com o estado $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle,$ obtemos uma expressão "
"semelhante, exceto que ela tem um $\\sqrt{2}$ no denominador:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our interest in this particular inner product will become clear shortly, but"
" for now we're simply observing this as a formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nosso interesse nesse produto interno específico ficará claro em breve, mas "
"por ora estamos simplesmente observando isso como uma fórmula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, define a unitary matrix $U_{\\theta}$ for each angle $\\theta$ as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, defina uma matriz unitária $U_{\\theta}$ para cada ângulo "
"$\\theta$ da seguinte forma.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this matrix transforms $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"To check that this is a unitary matrix, a key observation is that the vectors $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ are orthogonal for every angle $\\theta$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Intuitivamente falando, esta matriz transforma $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ em $\\vert 0\\rangle$ e $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ em $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Para verificar que esta é uma matriz unitária, uma observação fundamental é que os vetores $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ e $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ são ortogonais para todo ângulo $\\theta$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we find that\n"
msgstr "Portanto, encontramos que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We may alternatively write this matrix explicitly as\n"
msgstr "Podemos também escrever esta matriz explicitamente como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is an example of a *rotation matrix*, and specifically it rotates two-dimensional vectors with real number entries by an angle of $-\\theta$ about the origin.\n"
"If we follow a standard convention for naming and parameterizing rotations of various forms, we have\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"Este é um exemplo de uma *matriz de rotação*, e especificamente ela rotaciona vetores bidimensionais com entradas de números reais por um ângulo de $-\\theta$ em torno da origem.\n"
"Se seguirmos uma convenção padrão para nomear e parametrizar rotações de várias formas, temos\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ onde\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Strategy description {#strategy-description}"
msgstr "Descrição da estratégia {#strategy-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can describe the quantum strategy.\n"
msgstr "Agora podemos descrever a estratégia quântica.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Set-up:** Alice and Bob start the game sharing an e-bit: Alice holds a "
"qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the two "
"qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ are in the $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ "
"state.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Configuração:** Alice e Bob começam o jogo compartilhando um e-bit: Alice "
"possui um qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob possui um qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ e juntos "
"os dois qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ estão no estado "
"$\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Alice's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Ações de Alice:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question $x=0,$ she applies $U_{0}$ to her qubit "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Se Alice recebe a pergunta $x=0,$ ela aplica $U_{0}$ ao seu qubit "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question  $x=1,$ she applies $U_{\\pi/4}$ to her qubit"
" $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Se Alice recebe a pergunta $x=1,$ ela aplica $U_{\\pi/4}$ ao seu qubit "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The operation Alice performs on $\\mathsf{A}$ may alternatively be described like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  A operação que Alice realiza em $\\mathsf{A}$ pode ser descrita alternativamente assim:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Alice applies this operation, she measures $\\mathsf{A}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets her answer $a$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Depois que Alice aplica esta operação, ela mede $\\mathsf{A}$ com uma "
"medição na base padrão e define sua resposta $a$ como o resultado da "
"medição.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Bob's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Ações de Bob:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=0,$ he applies $U_{\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Se Bob recebe a pergunta $y=0,$ ele aplica $U_{\\pi/8}$ ao seu qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=1,$ he applies $U_{-\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Se Bob recebe a pergunta $y=1,$ ele aplica $U_{-\\pi/8}$ ao seu qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Like we did for Alice, we can express Bob's operation on $\\mathsf{B}$ like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Assim como fizemos para Alice, podemos expressar a operação de Bob em $\\mathsf{B}$ assim:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Bob applies this operation, he measures $\\mathsf{B}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets his answer $b$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Depois que Bob aplica esta operação, ele mede $\\mathsf{B}$ com uma "
"medição na base padrão e define sua resposta $b$ como o resultado da "
"medição.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit diagram that describes this strategy:\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui está um diagrama de circuito quântico que descreve esta estratégia:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/CHSH.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/CHSH.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this diagram we see two ordinary controlled gates, one for $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{\\pi/4}$ on the bottom.\n"
"We also have two gates that look like controlled gates, one for $U_{\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{0}$ on the bottom, except that the circle representing the control is not filled in.\n"
"This denotes a different type of controlled gate where the gate is performed if the control is set to $0$ (rather than $1$ like an ordinary controlled gate).\n"
"So, effectively, Bob performs $U_{\\pi/8}$ on his qubit if $y=0$ and $U_{-\\pi/8}$ if $y=1;$\n"
"and Alice performs $U_0$ on her qubit if $x=0$ and $U_{\\pi/4}$ if $x=1,$ which is consistent with the description of the protocol in words above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Neste diagrama vemos duas portas controladas comuns, uma para $U_{-\\pi/8}$ no topo e outra para $U_{\\pi/4}$ na parte inferior.\n"
"Também temos duas portas que parecem portas controladas, uma para $U_{\\pi/8}$ no topo e outra para $U_{0}$ na parte inferior, exceto que o círculo representando o controle não está preenchido.\n"
"Isso denota um tipo diferente de porta controlada onde a porta é executada se o controle estiver definido como $0$ (em vez de $1$ como uma porta controlada comum).\n"
"Portanto, efetivamente, Bob realiza $U_{\\pi/8}$ em seu qubit se $y=0$ e $U_{-\\pi/8}$ se $y=1;$\n"
"e Alice realiza $U_0$ em seu qubit se $x=0$ e $U_{\\pi/4}$ se $x=1,$ o que é consistente com a descrição do protocolo em palavras acima.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to figure out how well this strategy for Alice and Bob works.\n"
"We'll do this by going through the four possible question pairs individually.\n"
msgstr ""
"Resta descobrir quão bem essa estratégia para Alice e Bob funciona.\n"
"Faremos isso passando pelos quatro pares de perguntas possíveis individualmente.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case-by-case analysis {#case-by-case-analysis}"
msgstr "Análise caso a caso {#case-by-case-analysis}"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 1:  $(x,y) = (0,0).$\n"
msgstr "Caso 1:  $(x,y) = (0,0).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{0}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Neste caso Alice realiza $U_{0}$ em seu qubit e Bob realiza $U_{\\pi/8}$ "
"no dele, portanto o estado dos dois qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ após "
"eles realizarem suas operações é\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The probabilities for the four possible answer pairs $(a,b)$ are "
"therefore as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"   As probabilidades para os quatro pares de respostas possíveis $(a,b)$ são"
" portanto as seguintes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We can then obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by "
"summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Podemos então obter as probabilidades de que $a=b$ e $a\\neq b$ "
"somando.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(0,0),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ and therefore "
"they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para o par de perguntas $(0,0),$ Alice e Bob vencem se $a=b,$ e portanto "
"vencem neste caso com probabilidade\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 2:  $(x,y) = (0,1).$\n"
msgstr "Caso 2:  $(x,y) = (0,1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{0}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{-\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Neste caso Alice realiza $U_{0}$ em seu qubit e Bob realiza $U_{-\\pi/8}$"
" no dele, portanto o estado dos dois qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ após"
" eles realizarem suas operações é\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Again, we can obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by "
"summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Novamente, podemos obter as probabilidades de que $a=b$ e $a\\neq b$ "
"somando.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(0,1),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ and therefore "
"they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para o par de perguntas $(0,1),$ Alice e Bob vencem se $a=b,$ e portanto "
"vencem neste caso com probabilidade\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 3:  $(x,y) = (1,0).$\n"
msgstr "Caso 3:  $(x,y) = (1,0).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{\\pi/4}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Neste caso Alice realiza $U_{\\pi/4}$ em seu qubit e Bob realiza "
"$U_{\\pi/8}$ no dele, portanto o estado dos dois qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ após eles realizarem suas operações é\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We find, once again, that probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ are as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Encontramos, mais uma vez, que as probabilidades de que $a=b$ e $a\\neq "
"b$ são as seguintes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(1,0),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ so they win in"
" this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para o par de perguntas $(1,0),$ Alice e Bob vencem se $a=b,$ então "
"vencem neste caso com probabilidade\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 4:  $(x,y) = (1,1).$\n"
msgstr "Caso 4:  $(x,y) = (1,1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The last case is a little bit different, as we might expect because the "
"winning condition is different in this case. When $x$ and $y$ are both $1,$ "
"Alice and Bob win when $a$ and $b$ are *different*. In this case Alice "
"performs $U_{\\pi/4}$ on her qubit and Bob performs $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on his, so"
" the state of the two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform "
"their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   O último caso é um pouco diferente, como podemos esperar porque a "
"condição de vitória é diferente neste caso. Quando $x$ e $y$ são ambos $1,$ "
"Alice e Bob vencem quando $a$ e $b$ são *diferentes*. Neste caso Alice "
"realiza $U_{\\pi/4}$ em seu qubit e Bob realiza $U_{-\\pi/8}$ no dele, "
"portanto o estado dos dois qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ após eles "
"realizarem suas operações é\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The probabilities have effectively swapped places from in the three other cases.\n"
"   We obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   As probabilidades efetivamente trocaram de lugar em relação aos três outros casos.\n"
"   Obtemos as probabilidades de que $a=b$ e $a\\neq b$ somando.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(1,1),$ Alice and Bob win if $a\\neq b,$ and "
"therefore they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para o par de perguntas $(1,1),$ Alice e Bob vencem se $a\\neq b,$ e "
"portanto vencem neste caso com probabilidade\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "They win in every case with the same probability:\n"
msgstr "Eles vencem em todos os casos com a mesma probabilidade:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is therefore the probability that they win overall.\n"
"That's significantly better than any classical strategy can do for this game; classical strategies have winning probability bounded by $3/4.$ And that makes this a very interesting example.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta é portanto a probabilidade de eles vencerem no geral.\n"
"Isso é significativamente melhor do que qualquer estratégia clássica pode alcançar para este jogo; estratégias clássicas têm probabilidade de vitória limitada a $3/4.$ E isso torna este um exemplo muito interessante.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This happens to be the *optimal* winning probability for quantum strategies.\n"
"That is, we can't do any better than this, no matter what entangled state or measurements we choose.\n"
"This fact is known as *Tsirelson's inequality*, named for Boris Tsirelson who first proved it — and who first described the CHSH experiment as a game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta acontece ser a probabilidade de vitória *ótima* para estratégias quânticas.\n"
"Ou seja, não podemos fazer melhor do que isso, independentemente do estado entrelaçado ou das medições que escolhamos.\n"
"Este fato é conhecido como a *desigualdade de Tsirelson*, com o nome de Boris Tsirelson que a provou pela primeira vez — e que descreveu pela primeira vez o experimento CHSH como um jogo.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Geometric picture {#geometric-picture}"
msgstr "Visão geométrica {#geometric-picture}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is possible to think about the strategy described above geometrically, "
"which may be helpful for understanding the relationships among the various "
"angles chosen for Alice and Bob's operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"É possível pensar sobre a estratégia descrita acima geometricamente, o que "
"pode ser útil para entender as relações entre os vários ângulos escolhidos "
"para as operações de Alice e Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Alice effectively does is to choose an angle $\\alpha,$ depending on her question $x,$ and then to apply $U_{\\alpha}$ to her qubit and measure.\n"
"Similarly, Bob chooses an angle $\\beta,$ depending on $y,$ and then he applies $U_{\\beta}$ to his qubit and measures.\n"
"We've chosen $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ like so.\n"
msgstr ""
"O que Alice efetivamente faz é escolher um ângulo $\\alpha,$ dependendo de sua pergunta $x,$ e então aplicar $U_{\\alpha}$ ao seu qubit e medir.\n"
"Da mesma forma, Bob escolhe um ângulo $\\beta,$ dependendo de $y,$ e então aplica $U_{\\beta}$ ao seu qubit e mede.\n"
"Escolhemos $\\alpha$ e $\\beta$ da seguinte forma.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the moment, though, let's take $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ to be arbitrary.\n"
"By choosing $\\alpha,$ Alice effectively defines an orthonormal basis of vectors that looks like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Por enquanto, no entanto, vamos tomar $\\alpha$ e $\\beta$ como arbitrários.\n"
"Ao escolher $\\alpha,$ Alice efetivamente define uma base ortonormal de vetores que se parece com isso:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Basis for Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/alpha-basis.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Basis for Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/alpha-basis.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob does likewise, except that his angle is $\\beta$:\n"
msgstr "Bob faz o mesmo, exceto que seu ângulo é $\\beta$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Basis for Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/beta-basis.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Basis for Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/beta-basis.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The colors of the vectors correspond to Alice and Bob's answers: blue for "
"$0$ and red for $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"As cores dos vetores correspondem às respostas de Alice e Bob: azul para $0$"
" e vermelho para $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now, if we combine together $(1)$ and $(2)$ we get the formula\n"
msgstr "Agora, se combinarmos $(1)$ e $(2)$ obtemos a fórmula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which works for all real numbers $\\alpha$ and $\\beta.$\n"
msgstr "que funciona para todos os números reais $\\alpha$ e $\\beta.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following the same sort of analysis that we went through above, but with "
"$\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ being variables, we find this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Seguindo o mesmo tipo de análise que fizemos acima, mas com $\\alpha$ e "
"$\\beta$ sendo variáveis, encontramos isto:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We conclude these two formulas:\n"
msgstr "Concluímos estas duas fórmulas:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These equations can be connected to the figures above by imagining that we superimpose the bases chosen by Alice and Bob.\n"
"In particular, when $(x,y) = (0,0),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = \\pi/8,$ and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Essas equações podem ser conectadas às figuras acima imaginando que sobrepomos as bases escolhidas por Alice e Bob.\n"
"Em particular, quando $(x,y) = (0,0),$ Alice e Bob escolhem $\\alpha = 0$ e $\\beta = \\pi/8,$ e ao sobrepor suas bases obtemos esta figura:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy00.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy00.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angle between the red vectors is $\\pi/8,$ which is the same as the angle between the two blue vectors.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is the cosine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"O ângulo entre os vetores vermelhos é $\\pi/8,$ que é o mesmo que o ângulo entre os dois vetores azuis.\n"
"A probabilidade de que os resultados de Alice e Bob concordem é o cosseno ao quadrado deste ângulo,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "while the probability they disagree is the sine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"enquanto a probabilidade de discordarem é o seno ao quadrado deste ângulo,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (0,1),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8,$ and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Quando $(x,y) = (0,1),$ Alice e Bob escolhem $\\alpha = 0$ e $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8,$ e ao sobrepor suas bases obtemos esta figura:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy01.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy01.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angle between the red vectors is again $\\pi/8,$ as is the angle between the blue vectors.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is again the cosine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"O ângulo entre os vetores vermelhos é novamente $\\pi/8,$ assim como o ângulo entre os vetores azuis.\n"
"A probabilidade de que os resultados de Alice e Bob concordem é novamente o cosseno ao quadrado deste ângulo,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (1,0),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ and $\\beta = "
"\\pi/8,$ and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Quando $(x,y) = (1,0),$ Alice e Bob escolhem $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ e $\\beta = "
"\\pi/8,$ e ao sobrepor suas bases obtemos esta figura:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy10.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy10.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bases have changed but the angles haven't — once again the angle between vectors of the same color is $\\pi/8.$\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is\n"
msgstr ""
"As bases mudaram mas os ângulos não — mais uma vez o ângulo entre vetores da mesma cor é $\\pi/8.$\n"
"A probabilidade de que os resultados de Alice e Bob concordem é\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and the probability they disagree is\n"
msgstr "e a probabilidade de discordarem é\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (1,1),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ and $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8.$ When we superimpose their bases, we see that something different "
"has happened:\n"
msgstr ""
"Quando $(x,y) = (1,1),$ Alice e Bob escolhem $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ e $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8.$ Quando sobrepomos suas bases, vemos que algo diferente "
"aconteceu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy11.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy11.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the way the angles were chosen, this time the angle between vectors having the same color is $3\\pi/8$ rather than $\\pi/8.$\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is still the cosine-squared of this angle, but this time the value is\n"
msgstr ""
"Pela forma como os ângulos foram escolhidos, desta vez o ângulo entre vetores com a mesma cor é $3\\pi/8$ em vez de $\\pi/8.$\n"
"A probabilidade de que os resultados de Alice e Bob concordem ainda é o cosseno ao quadrado deste ângulo, mas desta vez o valor é\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probability the outcomes disagree is the sine-squared of this angle, "
"which in this case is this:\n"
msgstr ""
"A probabilidade de os resultados discordarem é o seno ao quadrado deste "
"ângulo, que neste caso é:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remarks {#remarks}"
msgstr "Observações {#remarks}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The basic idea of an experiment like the CHSH game, where entanglement leads to statistical results that are inconsistent with purely classical reasoning, is due to John Bell, the namesake of the Bell states.\n"
"For this reason, people often refer to experiments of this sort as *Bell tests*.\n"
"Sometimes people also refer to *Bell's theorem*, which can be formulated in different ways — but the essence of it is that quantum mechanics is not compatible with so-called *local hidden variable theories*.\n"
"The CHSH game is a particularly clean and simple example of a Bell test, and can be viewed as a proof, or demonstration, of Bell's theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"A ideia básica de um experimento como o jogo CHSH, onde o entrelaçamento leva a resultados estatísticos que são inconsistentes com o raciocínio puramente clássico, é devida a John Bell, o patrono dos estados de Bell.\n"
"Por essa razão, as pessoas frequentemente se referem a experimentos desse tipo como *testes de Bell*.\n"
"Às vezes as pessoas também se referem ao *teorema de Bell*, que pode ser formulado de diferentes maneiras — mas a essência dele é que a mecânica quântica não é compatível com as chamadas *teorias de variáveis ocultas locais*.\n"
"O jogo CHSH é um exemplo particularmente limpo e simples de um teste de Bell, e pode ser visto como uma prova, ou demonstração, do teorema de Bell.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game offers a way to experimentally test the theory of quantum information.\n"
"Experiments can be performed that implement the CHSH game, and test the sorts of strategies based on entanglement described above.\n"
"This provides us with a high degree of confidence that entanglement is real — and unlike the sometimes vague or poetic ways that we come up with to explain entanglement, the CHSH game gives us a concrete and testable way to *observe* entanglement.\n"
"The 2022 Nobel Prize in Physics acknowledges the importance of this line of work: the prize was awarded to Alain Aspect, John Clauser (the C in CHSH) and Anton Zeilinger for observing entanglement through Bell tests on entangled photons.\n"
msgstr ""
"O jogo CHSH oferece uma maneira de testar experimentalmente a teoria da informação quântica.\n"
"Experimentos podem ser realizados que implementam o jogo CHSH e testam os tipos de estratégias baseadas em entrelaçamento descritas acima.\n"
"Isso nos fornece um alto grau de confiança de que o entrelaçamento é real — e ao contrário das formas às vezes vagas ou poéticas que criamos para explicar o entrelaçamento, o jogo CHSH nos dá uma maneira concreta e testável de *observar* o entrelaçamento.\n"
"O Prêmio Nobel de Física de 2022 reconhece a importância desta linha de trabalho: o prêmio foi concedido a Alain Aspect, John Clauser (o C em CHSH) e Anton Zeilinger por observar o entrelaçamento através de testes de Bell em fótons entrelaçados.\n"
